<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Dujana State</h1><p class="st-meta">1806 CE – 1948 CE · capital Dujana</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A tiny Pathan Nawabi state in Haryana, granted by the British in 1806 to a cavalry leader who had served them against the Marathas.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdul-samad-khan-of-dujana">Abdul Samad Khan</a>, a Pathan soldier, served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gerard-lake-1st-viscount-lake">Lord Lake</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-anglo-maratha-war">Second Anglo-Maratha War</a>, and in 1806 the British granted him Dujana and its villages as a hereditary state.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Nawabs governed a very small farming territory under British supervision through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> government. Little is recorded of its internal history.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Dujana acceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and in 1948 was merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-punjab">East Punjab</a>; it lies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jhajjar">Jhajjar</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haryana">Haryana</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="princely state, 1806 CE – 1948 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">princely state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Indian princely states</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:95.64%;width:2.83%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1806 CE – 1948 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dujana</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abdul Samad Khan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism; Sunni Islam (ruling house)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Haryanvi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>India</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dujana</dd></dl></aside></div>
